{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1564"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge film-media/film","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/film-media__film.g3.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",590],["+","Twelve years later Redford directed „A River Runs Through It“ (1992), Norman Maclean's story of two brothers fly-fishing in Montana, and cast a young Brad Pitt as the gifted, reckless younger brother Paul; critics remarked on his resemblance to the young Redford so often that Pitt was soon called his heir, and the two later played mentor and protégé in „Spy Game“ (2001). Pitt's next big part had political consequences: after he played the Austrian mountaineer Heinrich Harrer in Jean-Jacques Annaud's „Seven Years in Tibet“ (1997), a film sympathetic to the Dalai Lama, China barred him, the director and his co-star David Thewlis from entering the country; Pitt was able to visit again only in 2014.\n\n"],["=",386],["+","A River Runs Through It (director) | 1992 | Brad Pitt |\n| "],["=",47]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",552],["+","Zwölf Jahre später inszenierte Redford „Aus der Mitte entspringt ein Fluss“ (1992), Norman Macleans Geschichte zweier Brüder beim Fliegenfischen in Montana, und besetzte den jungen Brad Pitt als begabten, leichtsinnigen jüngeren Bruder Paul; Kritiker bemerkten so oft seine Ähnlichkeit mit dem jungen Redford, dass Pitt bald als sein Erbe galt, und in „Spy Game – Der finale Countdown“ (2001) spielten die beiden Mentor und Schützling. Pitts nächste große Rolle hatte politische Folgen: Nachdem er in Jean-Jacques Annauds „Sieben Jahre in Tibet“ (1997), einem dem Dalai Lama wohlgesonnenen Film, den österreichischen Bergsteiger Heinrich Harrer gespielt hatte, verweigerte China ihm, dem Regisseur und seinem Kollegen David Thewlis die Einreise; erst 2014 konnte Pitt das Land wieder besuchen.\n\n"],["=",362],["+","Aus der Mitte entspringt ein Fluss (Regie) | 1992 | Brad Pitt |\n| "],["=",47]]}]},
